#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119574 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "a6fded96-287a-53ee-8b1c-dd618562b2c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4940" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{p}+ s\\mathbf{b}+ t \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,5 \\rangle,$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-3,2,5⟩+s\\,⟨17,3,15⟩+t\\,⟨5,0,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "297bda8f-6e33-5cc2-a2e1-5ab6186fa9d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4941" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(2,50,-19)$ and is parallel to the lines $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 2,\\sqrt{6},17 \\rangle + s \\langle -1,7,2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 20,-44, 27 \\rangle + t \\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle  -1,7,2  \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(2,50,-19)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,50,-19 \\rangle.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨2,50,-19⟩+s\\,⟨-1,7,2⟩+t\\,⟨2\\sqrt{3},9,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119576 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/id #uuid "9c36ddd5-fcf1-5c4d-a350-aa8ef3a3ca9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4942" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119588 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "b86eace4-01cb-5601-8e9b-2658e81fc656" :question/math-academy-id "e-5884" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}= \\langle -6,3, 2 \\rangle + t \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle + s \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle,\\qquad t,\\,s \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{w} = \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-12j-20k \\\\  & =⟨1,-12,-20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 1, -12, -20 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54cc13d1-3c01-5c94-931a-746f4e769751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384549} {:answer/id #uuid "21c82870-e73c-57b5-8b82-c6f315502aef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-4,3⟩+s⟨2,5,-1⟩+t⟨2,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384550} {:answer/id #uuid "a1134b55-777d-553b-a5ca-4406e939a89c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,4,-3⟩+s⟨5,-1,1⟩+t⟨2.5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384551} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb6557e-0654-5ba0-8124-c584b214b309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-2,4⟩+s⟨1,-5,-1⟩+t⟨1,1,2.5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384552} {:answer/id #uuid "44615d5d-47b3-598e-9d82-2e26f22cb599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,1,-1⟩+t⟨1,4.5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54cc13d1-3c01-5c94-931a-746f4e769751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384549} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cfa854f-8134-59c5-b3ab-2a05b1747d86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9a73f23-a384-52a5-9c21-2b77145a980d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128464" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨1,5,-1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,2.5,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,5,-1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,2.5,1⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "944e707d-89e4-580f-aba7-7d8ee794464e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312071} {:answer/id #uuid "1830beae-83d0-505d-832d-f8be1c218587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312072} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c09f52-377f-56d4-b795-b3452fac5be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312073} {:answer/id #uuid "25bc43e3-849b-5f52-b947-b8f74e046cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312074} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6f9a04-8dfd-5705-8af9-b2ffe6fe1e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7c09f52-377f-56d4-b795-b3452fac5be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312073} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ca3e02-6674-5400-87a6-6cf8fa389de8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9e20786-5f2c-55c6-bc0f-010879e57039" :question/math-academy-id "q-128467" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $S(1,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $S$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c394f154-7da4-5fd6-8df5-0f0b623511a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-19,-1,17⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384556} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e163a8-07d4-5e85-88ed-24901741d946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,1,-13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384557} {:answer/id #uuid "c60132e4-4f3d-5301-8926-bd6612d7f026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-3,-23⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384558} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b5d1fc-7a74-5c37-95d1-a8caa240e41f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,3,-21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384559} {:answer/id #uuid "0c037ba7-7eb0-5242-84b2-3bf2f2cc670e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,-1,-23⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c037ba7-7eb0-5242-84b2-3bf2f2cc670e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,-1,-23⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384560} :answer-field/id #uuid "90626423-cba2-5556-af40-71c5125c3758" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a5f5619e-e530-5907-b493-6149f34e2c31" :question/math-academy-id "q-128495" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,7,-2⟩+t⟨-3,4,1⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩$ and $w=⟨5,1,-2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-9i-j-23k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384561 :kn