parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91ac9edb-fec4-5707-be50-fcbb480cf666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,5⟩+t⟨3,6,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312078} {:answer/id #uuid "aabeb61e-b320-529d-8444-6279bb150f50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,2⟩+t⟨4,3,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312079} {:answer/id #uuid "1974de00-d585-539d-bb79-d49fae942a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-7,3⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨3,5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312080} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a4e0cf-df0a-5da4-8318-83716ae162ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312081} {:answer/id #uuid "9639e8c5-a54f-5c6a-8405-3aa2b7d9068c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,2⟩+s⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨7,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a4e0cf-df0a-5da4-8318-83716ae162ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312081} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64c26b3-76ef-5a06-88aa-856bcfb352cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d8e167e-ba7b-5746-8896-10f0f88087c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128501" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2296ee22-29c4-5cad-913e-95d4426da320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384570} {:answer/id #uuid "883287e2-a22a-5866-9f86-3af322e4f5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨1,-2,-1⟩+t⟨5,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384571} {:answer/id #uuid "f27b04e6-394d-5f9a-9844-f6c14698c3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,-2⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384572} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee9aec9-fb7e-5250-ace8-f082136c792a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,1,2⟩+t⟨-3,1,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384573} {:answer/id #uuid "66ed9ad4-457c-5194-b232-9583f0a305c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66ed9ad4-457c-5194-b232-9583f0a305c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384574} :answer-field/id #uuid "d767602d-d48d-597f-988f-cbe8628ba9a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8ae8a52-91d4-5f03-bbaf-4e5a85108c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-128741" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(1,-2,3),\\,Q(3,-4,2),$ and $R(4,3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-4,2⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨4,3,2⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨1,-2,3⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77f70ab9-df05-5d06-8368-1847ce4eb05b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312099} {:answer/id #uuid "190189ce-b4a1-5c28-b4a6-84251bb0f27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,2,4⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312100} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfd55f1-d72c-53c3-940e-c30413943ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312101} {:answer/id #uuid "94004271-92e2-5a26-9cc9-b798a13c8b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,4,2⟩+t⟨4,-4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312102} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8dd248-653a-5444-a799-dc1b572980a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨4,2,6⟩+t⟨-4,-3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77f70ab9-df05-5d06-8368-1847ce4eb05b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312099} :answer-field/id #uuid "efe908a8-da17-59c3-a7de-9fca8a1238e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59e11878-2a74-52d6-b175-2dda09601ebd" :question/math-academy-id "q-128760" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "824d34c2-11d0-543a-bd5f-69b14b4e3bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨ - 2, 23, 14⟩ + s⟨ - 3, 5, 4⟩ + t⟨4, 7,-1⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117535} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb8b09c-0270-5f95-85e9-39e632fcc31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨ - 2, 23, 14⟩ + s⟨ - 3, 5, 1⟩ + t⟨ - 30, 55, 25⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117536} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb33ad5-c788-5cd7-afd3-0cb1255c33a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨ - 3, 5, 4⟩ + s⟨ - 2, 23, 14⟩ + t⟨4, 7,-1⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117537} {:answer/id #uuid "0f30deb8-d2fd-51e7-9013-2939cda7b68b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117538} {:answer/id #uuid "6f4e8477-e00d-5168-ba43-abc0b6634f37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨ - 2, 23, 14⟩ + s⟨ - 3, 5, 1⟩ + t⟨4, 7,-1⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824d34c2-11d0-543a-bd5f-69b14b4e3bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨ - 2, 23, 14⟩ + s⟨ - 3, 5, 4⟩ + t⟨4, 7,-1⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117535} :answer-field/id #uuid "adfeb1bb-d319-549b-9a79-4c69e21c0e3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88872368-686b-5e7f-9016-e33ff5ee0ad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33158" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-2,23,14)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-3,5,1⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $r=⟨-30,55,25⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨4,7,-1⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-2,23,14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-2,23,14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84e4c26f-ad44-590f-9ab1-12c942e03908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 59, 10,-20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117767} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ecfe6b-3641-54e8-9533-754a42060b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 2,-7, 5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117768} {:answer/id #uuid "eb99b711-2d3a-5b24-b63d-7c837293a262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 95, 20,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117769} {:answer/id #uuid "146d4e0e-2bb7-5867-9df9-6b32549b1c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 4,-84, 25⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117770} {:answer/id #uuid "450b04e0-c5f4-5f17-a2b6-4065caa08239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2, 0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb99b711-2d3a-5b24-b63d-7c837293a262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 95, 20,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117769} :answer-field/id #uuid "57779420-4092-5133-8afc-9db48310bdd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "183d75ab-bc55-5284-9356-4879f8cd6310" :question/math-academy-id "q-33818" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,0,-1⟩+t⟨-2,-7,5⟩+s⟨2,12,5⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,-7,5⟩$ and $w=⟨2,12,5⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-95i+20j-10k \\\\  & =⟨-95,20,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-95,20,-10⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c9cbea4-9456-56c2-b99f-093694fae63e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,21,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312127} {:answer/id #uuid "c475d69a-3f07-5211-9dac-db46fe94d0a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-33,13,-41⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312128} {:answer/id #uuid "1de7290d-b180-5d55-93d9-cfc4291629df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,5,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312129} {:answer/id #uuid "a98f57c0-5b3e-55af-9829-975a2097c417" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-13,33,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312130} {:answer/id #uuid "5afea236-e140-5820-9ef5-b834153781bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,7,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c475d69a-3f07-5211-9dac-db46fe94d0a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-33,13,-41⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312128} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a4a236-d7ae-5a15-9d18-d073626bb864" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f234c8a-5296-59f1-9978-57c05cbc1be8" :question/math-academy-id "q-33819" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 23 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $w=⟨4,7,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-33i+13j-41k \\\\  & =⟨-33,13,-41⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-33,13,-41⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0543e47d-e3ac-5ccd-9244-70eaf00bbafd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,13,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312141} {:answer/id #uuid "5277c0f7-53ef-5846-b406-7ea29a3181e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312142} {:answer/id #uuid "c26420c2-ef3b-5769-94eb-32335cd21d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312143} {:answer/id #uuid "905c9369-6ad8-5fe8-9315-75957dd90738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312144} {:answer/id #uuid "af529e89-f16d-560a-bbc1-27393a0b40f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-7,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af529e89-f16d-560a-bbc1-27393a0b40f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-7,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312145} :answer-field/id #uuid "90137fc2-dc53-5b09-9971-16682329f8d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51de2ebd-845c-5a52-9ff3-452c3613ef46" :question/math-academy-id "q-33822" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-5,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,1,-2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-3i-7j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f689df-8a7b-59a0-92b5-d8d827a3afd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384577} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb58648-450b-57ad-b82e-6410b8a93adb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384578} {:answer/id #uuid "22da6319-1506-581f-896e-c07fc0e69f69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384579} {:answer/id #uuid "accaa354-a417-521c-b6c8-7f7641e45964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,0,4⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384580} {:answer/id #uuid "0155cfeb-7ca1-5934-ae63-db8b692601a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-4,1⟩+s⟨-1,0,4⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "accaa354-a417-521c-b6c8-7f7641e45964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,0,4⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384580} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f4d6760-3a4d-5037-9f7e-da6a8b1ee3bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "751c263d-74fc-5bd0-966f-c7cfdf00bcf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-70965" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-1,0,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $Q$ is $p=⟨-1,0,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1,0,4⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a2686ea-6935-5f28-b5a3-bfca91494284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384584} {:answer/id #uuid "8181d921-1a85-542a-822e-36d04f627f3f" :