\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $S$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd6d69c1-3543-542a-aab3-8d631191f912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312155} {:answer/id #uuid "8eeb52e0-d9bb-52a8-bb89-2e22ad9cc436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312156} {:answer/id #uuid "0c121cba-a491-5e96-aecd-e3d38f0d5ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=s[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312157} {:answer/id #uuid "881a9287-3a76-5d68-855f-53826af674fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} 