) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d16ac501-66f8-52cd-8aa9-032b3a35da71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312169} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f4b402-6e07-59fd-be95-cd005d2a69f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312170} {:answer/id #uuid "659cd2e2-7cd4-53fd-9d6b-1f0d37e3db5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312171} {:answer/id #uuid "5e631b40-1ef7-5a95-9e42-dad35f111830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312172} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc6bd90-10d7-55f9-a911-c93b97815b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4f4b402-6e07-59fd-be95-cd005d2a69f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312170} :answer-field/id #uuid "89d420fe-daef-5abc-8dbf-88f7a32c4916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a89b1eb9-5618-5992-98db-513e5d1c24f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-70972" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨0,-1,3⟩$ and $w=⟨1,2,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65db0400-cb51-5d1c-95bc-13b40540e6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384591} {:answer/id #uuid "c7164b4a-10ca-55f8-90a8-29f0a6e48dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384592} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd42a51-87db-5444-a542-250cdefdd488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,0,3⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384593} {:answer/id #uuid "628f16d5-4c7c-5663-81c5-ace18aa15b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,2,-3⟩+s⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384594} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c69f1-e39d-58cd-a058-b54a076c1d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨0,11,\\frac{1}{3}⟩+t⟨0,\\sqrt{2},5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7164b4a-10ca-55f8-90a8-29f0a6e48dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384592} :answer-field/id #uuid "446c8cfe-5df2-5c5b-9dde-e9903f8903ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8741dd2e-af66-5ff8-a395-814964cd05f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-70976" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨0,11,\\frac{1}{3}⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩$ and $r=⟨0,\\sqrt{2},5⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,2,-3⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨-1,0,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9bcaf6c-22b5-5a20-aba0-16f35d322295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,1,-2⟩+s⟨16,-1,3⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312183} {:answer/id #uuid "d11e3e9a-7b9a-540e-a540-76c8379fcc9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312184} {:answer/id #uuid "40b0d2e2-d535-5a49-9062-ad4abf81c091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312185} {:answer/id #uuid "1066ae23-c95d-5779-8139-35445e112b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨9,-7,2⟩+t⟨15,2,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312186} {:answer/id #uuid "c5670c2e-d06a-524b-8c54-2a3d5e717368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,11,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨16,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40b0d2e2-d535-5a49-9062-ad4abf81c091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312185} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9d7f215-88a8-5742-98dd-d45731dfaeab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1380b7ab-2f50-57d6-bb5c-11a707fc3968" :question/math-academy-id "q-70978" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $E(16,-1,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,-7,2⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩$ and $r=⟨15,2,-3⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨5,1,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,11,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $E(16,-1,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $e=⟨16,-1,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =e+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36caaaa3-a3a5-5d6d-9ded-c34b55210909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384598} {:answer/id #uuid "05337fd0-5c24-5739-9dcf-012038b535a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨2,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,-8,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384599} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8811e0-0ee1-5d65-b136-4d82e4af4375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384600} {:answer/id #uuid "2cbfa485-c371-541c-8c96-5c8f9ee1a9c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨1,-7,-2⟩+t⟨0,-8,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384601} {:answer/id #uuid "0e0c05af-0ddb-5517-aecc-83ec6f697a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed8811e0-0ee1-5d65-b136-4d82e4af4375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384600} :answer-field/id #uuid "8def66d5-9c17-597c-bd95-012a8c0d2339" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e75ca09-55e0-56a4-85df-a6bfc7789b73" :question/math-academy-id "q-71034" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $L(-1,-1,1),\\,M(2,5,-3)$, and $N(0,-8,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =⟨2,5,-3⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =⟨0,-8,-1⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $l=⟨-1,-1,1⟩$ of the point $l,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =l+s\\overset{\\to }{LM}+t\\overset{\\to }{LN} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f3e43e1-3762-52bc-bf68-8e5a138ca345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨2,-9,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384605} {:answer/id #uuid "af581e99-f8df-5617-85c8-cc7b5791afab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384606} {:answer/id #uuid "52e845ba-ddb5-530f-bdd3-3435f18edd50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384607} {:answer/id #uuid "ac4ce038-a717-5c0d-b4a4-6d2f8678acad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨0,-6,-1⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384608} {:answer/id #uuid "8055be52-6052-5055-8660-0041ac28c2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨2,-9,0⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52e845ba-ddb5-530f-bdd3-3435f18edd50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384607} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec937a83-4e84-5b53-9ec3-8cafc21ea228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "901f1360-df93-5e5e-ac60-c5607de4f628" :question/math-academy-id "q-71036" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(3,6,2),\\,Q(2,-9,0)$, and $R(3,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,-9,0⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-15,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨3,0,1⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨3,6,2⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f606e85e-cff2-5a26-8299-f11bc5f1cbe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :a